WEBVTT

NOTE Cue timings are estimated from sentence length and pauses in the audio.

1
00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:04.727
Welcome to the Tueri Systems Risk Brief for Wednesday, October twenty-eighth.

2
00:00:04.727 --> 00:00:07.557
Operational clarity when conditions change.

3
00:00:07.557 --> 00:00:12.205
A few minutes on what is happening, what can be confirmed, and what has changed.

4
00:00:12.205 --> 00:00:13.780
Digitally narrated.

5
00:00:13.780 --> 00:00:17.753
Cyclone Arnab has made landfall in India and is weakening.

6
00:00:17.753 --> 00:00:22.046
Saudi Arabia reports more interceptions, including over Riyadh.

7
00:00:22.046 --> 00:00:25.772
Gulf shipping has new guidance on the US blockade of Iran.

8
00:00:25.772 --> 00:00:28.663
And more countries have added Ebola entry measures.

9
00:00:28.663 --> 00:00:31.165
Here's the detail.

10
00:00:31.165 --> 00:00:32.094
India first.

11
00:00:32.094 --> 00:00:42.890
Reported, citing the India Meteorological Department: Cyclone Arnab crossed the Andhra Pradesh coast early Wednesday local time, Tuesday evening Central, as a very severe cyclonic storm.

12
00:00:42.890 --> 00:00:46.474
It has since weakened and is forecast to keep weakening inland.

13
00:00:46.474 --> 00:00:52.577
Reported: officials say at least three people have died and about fifty-seven thousand are in relief camps.

14
00:00:52.577 --> 00:01:00.888
Indian media report flights suspended at three Andhra Pradesh airports, dozens of trains cancelled, and power only partly restored.

15
00:01:00.888 --> 00:01:06.323
Teams on that coast should confirm road, rail and airport status before moving.

16
00:01:06.323 --> 00:01:07.646
Saudi Arabia.

17
00:01:07.646 --> 00:01:15.455
Reported: the Saudi-led coalition says it intercepted three ballistic missiles aimed at the Eastern Province and two over Riyadh.

18
00:01:15.455 --> 00:01:21.714
Saudi civil defense says falling debris in Riyadh damaged a building, a construction site and a vehicle.

19
00:01:21.714 --> 00:01:24.987
Alerts were later reported around Jeddah and Yanbu.

20
00:01:24.987 --> 00:01:30.888
Claim only: the Houthis say a missile hit the Ras Tanura refinery and caused major fires.

21
00:01:30.888 --> 00:01:33.306
Saudi Arabia has not confirmed that.

22
00:01:33.306 --> 00:01:42.807
Britain's Foreign Office has updated its advice for Saudi Arabia and more than a dozen other countries in the region, and now says the risk of sudden escalation is high.

23
00:01:42.807 --> 00:01:48.485
At Riyadh's main airport, Flightradar twenty-four data at about five thirty a.m.

24
00:01:48.485 --> 00:01:55.794
Central showed about seventeen percent of today's flights cancelled, against twenty-three percent at the same time yesterday on a similar schedule.

25
00:01:55.794 --> 00:01:57.988
One day's change is not a trend.

26
00:01:57.988 --> 00:02:02.294
It remains a partial reopening with observed disruption.

27
00:02:02.294 --> 00:02:03.246
Shipping.

28
00:02:03.246 --> 00:02:09.294
Confirmed: the Joint Maritime Information Center has issued an advisory note on the US blockade of Iranian ports.

29
00:02:09.294 --> 00:02:11.502
The blockade itself is not new.

30
00:02:11.502 --> 00:02:20.408
US naval forces say vessels moving between neutral ports in the Gulf of Oman and the Strait of Hormuz may be questioned, visited and searched.

31
00:02:20.408 --> 00:02:28.727
Ships should keep a radio watch, follow US directions, have signed cargo and port documents ready, and plan extra transit time.

32
00:02:28.727 --> 00:02:32.643
Vessels that do not need to transit are advised to stay well clear.

33
00:02:32.643 --> 00:02:37.615
The center's latest weekly assessment rates the threat in the Strait of Hormuz as severe.

34
00:02:37.615 --> 00:02:45.682
Reported: Iran's new strait authority says vessels it links to a South Korean tanker operator face legal action from November first.

35
00:02:45.682 --> 00:02:48.521
A Korean shipowners' group disputes that link.

36
00:02:48.521 --> 00:02:53.189
No new UK Maritime Trade Operations incident warning was found this cycle.

37
00:02:53.189 --> 00:02:56.770
That does not mean the threat has eased.

38
00:02:56.770 --> 00:02:57.738
Borders and health.

39
00:02:57.738 --> 00:03:10.167
Confirmed: Nigeria's Centre for Disease Control now requires every international arrival, including Nigerian citizens and crew, to complete a health declaration before boarding, with temperature screening on arrival.

40
00:03:10.167 --> 00:03:16.740
Reported, per the US Embassy in Abuja: arrivals could face quarantine or self-isolation of at least twenty-one days.

41
00:03:16.740 --> 00:03:29.637
Reported, per Britain's Foreign Office: El Salvador now requires a twenty-one-day quarantine for travelers who were in eight African countries, including Kenya, Uganda and Congo, in the previous twenty-one days.

42
00:03:29.637 --> 00:03:36.112
Already in force and unchanged: the US limits on travel from Congo, Uganda and South Sudan, and the US attestation rule from November third.

43
00:03:36.112 --> 00:03:43.267
Tueri suggests checking travel history against every country on a route, not only the first.

44
00:03:43.267 --> 00:03:44.717
Operations check.

45
00:03:44.717 --> 00:03:53.882
Internet: Georgia Tech's outage measurements show Crimea and Sevastopol back to about ninety-six percent of their reference levels, a recovery in the measured signal.

46
00:03:53.882 --> 00:04:02.628
In Bangladesh, a national grid fault cut power to eastern Dhaka and parts of the southeast on Tuesday, and Cloudflare saw traffic fall by up to a quarter.

47
00:04:02.628 --> 00:04:09.788
The grid operator says power was restored within about two hours; recovery for all users was not independently measured.

48
00:04:09.788 --> 00:04:13.190
Moscow's announced mobile internet limits run through Thursday.

49
00:04:13.190 --> 00:04:17.792
Power: Sudan's southeastern grid is not confirmed restored.

50
00:04:17.792 --> 00:04:22.119
Hazards: Nepal's authorities warn of heavy rain and snow from Thursday through Saturday.

51
00:04:22.119 --> 00:04:26.555
Other domains as above.

52
00:04:26.555 --> 00:04:28.356
That's today's brief.

53
00:04:28.356 --> 00:04:29.755
Current as of five fifty-five a.m.

54
00:04:29.755 --> 00:04:33.199
Central, Wednesday, with Nigeria's entry rules rechecked at seven a.m.

55
00:04:33.199 --> 00:04:38.485
Tueri summarizes public reporting.

56
00:04:38.485 --> 00:04:42.980
It is not legal, medical, or security advice for any specific situation.

57
00:04:42.980 --> 00:04:45.376
Check the original source before you act.

58
00:04:45.376 --> 00:04:54.439
Tueri Systems provides information verification, communications support, and operational decision support for organizations working in changing conditions.

59
00:04:54.439 --> 00:04:57.044
Learn more at tuerisystems.com.

60
00:04:57.044 --> 00:04:58.270
Thanks for listening.
